// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5892 Add New AppLocker Policy File Tampering Detection Rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5892
// Pull request author: raginx
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Deletion of AppLocker Policy Files
// Sigma ID: f2a8c3e4-1d5b-4a9c-8f6e-2b3c7d8a9f1e
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Reinhard Westerholt
// Date: 2026-03-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685.002
// Description: Detects suspicious deletion of AppLocker policy files which may indicate tampering or attempts
//   to disable application control.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators re-applying or repairing an AppLocker policy from a shell or script
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/security/threat-protection/applocker/applocker-overview
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4fdab67410a3655cfe80c318ba6459762f4ce386/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_susp_applocker_policy_deletion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType =~ "FileDeleted" and (FolderPath contains "\\System32\\AppLocker\\" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\python.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe"))
